# The in-tree build backend has to travel inside the sdist.
#
# `python -m build` makes the sdist first and then builds the wheel FROM that
# sdist. pyproject.toml names `backend-path = ["_build"]`, and setuptools only
# packages what it discovers under src/, so without this line the sdist has no
# _build/ directory and the wheel build dies with:
#   `backend-path` entry '_build' does not exist or is not a directory
# Measured in CI on 0bfcdf8, run 34881529560, on the build step and on all three
# acceptance jobs. Every local build in the lane used `python -m build --wheel`,
# which builds straight from the source tree and never makes an sdist, which is
# why nothing caught it before CI did.
include _build/backend.py
